Name:           barmbu
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        1%{?dist}
Summary:        Run Bambu Studio's official network plugin on ARM64 Linux

License:        GPL-3.0-or-later
URL:            https://github.com/amruthwo/barmbu
Source0:        %{name}-%{version}.tar.gz

BuildArch:      noarch
BuildRequires:  make

Requires:       python3 >= 3.9
Requires:       python3-gobject
Requires:       gtk4
Requires:       libadwaita
Requires:       squashfs-tools
Requires:       erofs-utils
Requires:       cpio
Requires:       rpm
Recommends:     fex-emu
Recommends:     muvm
Recommends:     fex-emu-rootfs-fedora

%description
A small app (window + command line) that gets Bambu Lab's official network
plugin working on ARM64 Linux, such as Apple Silicon Macs running Asahi.

Bambu only builds the plugin for x86_64, so on ARM64 the app sets up an
x86_64 copy of Bambu Studio that runs under FEX-Emu (inside muvm on 16K-page
kernels), adds the WebKit libraries it needs from Fedora's own x86_64
packages, and installs the official plugin. On x86_64 it just installs the
plugin. It uses Bambu's unmodified plugin, which signs in with its own
built-in credentials.

%prep
%setup -q

%build
# Pure Python; nothing to compile.

%install
make install-files DESTDIR=%{buildroot} PREFIX=%{_prefix}

%files
%{_bindir}/barmbu
%{_bindir}/barmbu-gui
%{_datadir}/barmbu/
%{_datadir}/applications/io.github.amruthwo.Barmbu.desktop
%{_datadir}/metainfo/io.github.amruthwo.Barmbu.metainfo.xml
%{_datadir}/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/io.github.amruthwo.Barmbu.svg
%doc %{_docdir}/%{name}/README.md
%license %{_docdir}/%{name}/LICENSE

%changelog
* Wed Nov 25 2026 amruthwo <amruthwo@users.noreply.github.com> - @VERSION@-1
- Graphical app, muvm support for Asahi, automatic WebKit add-on.
